    "result_text": "All 26 tests pass. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n**What I changed** \u2014 `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java`:\n\nThe `customerCode` now follows `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`:\n- `CITY3` \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of `city`\n- `LAST3` \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`\n- `NNNN` \u2014 a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence: one more than the owners already in that city (counted via `findAll()` filtered by city, case-insensitively, before this owner is saved).\n\n**Values derived from `customerCode` rebuild automatically.** The `membershipNumber` in `OwnerMapper` is `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", owner.getCustomerCode(), ...)` \u2014 it reads `getCustomerCode()` directly, so it now emits the city-prefixed form with no change needed (e.g. `SYD-SMI-0001-M26`). The `Cp14` test recomputes it from returned fields and confirms this.\n\nI kept the existing single-endpoint structure, `@Val`-in-place mutation, and pre-save counting semantics from the original function per the AGENTS.md conventions; only the format and the count's scope (global \u2192 per-city) changed. I also updated the class Javadoc to describe the new format.\n\nTest results: `Tests run: 26, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
